  "rationale": "The eight-strategy 2400-tick sweep, and the one where raids change what a strategy is. portal-rush went from a bot whose defining action was permanently masked to one that opens portals, assigns raiders and carries books home from universes that permitted cells this one forbids; every other strategy is now raided several times a run and loses shelved grimoires to fire. Grimoires fall 362 (-3.76 SE) and living mages 7.8. The new numbers are right because the old ones were recorded on a build where openPortal had zero candidates in every tick of every run -- the pre-raid figures measure the portal action being unreachable, not the raid economy.",
